This package is a standalone port of dsh-notification by omdsh-dev, used under
the MIT License. The original project lives at:

    https://github.com/omdsh-dev/dsh-notification

Upstream ships TypeScript sources, so this is a port rather than a repackage.
The behaviour is unchanged — the host registers the `notification` session
projection, and the browser half watches the session list, applies the
persisted rules, and calls the Notification API. The differences are packaging
and this repository's conventions:

  - Renamed to @my-dsh/notification. The client bundle's __ModuleLoader__ id
    follows, because the web boot manifest looks a bundle up by the installed
    package name. The projection key stays `notification`: it is the seam's
    key, not a package identity.

  - English only. Upstream carries a Simplified Chinese dictionary as the
    key-set source of truth with English mirroring it. This repository writes
    English only, so the English dictionary is now the source of truth and is
    registered under both locale ids — selecting Chinese leaves the harness in
    Chinese and this section in English, rather than rendering raw message
    keys from an unregistered namespace.

  - One type fix. `observedTurn` was declared `Map<string, number>` while
    `state.ids` carries a branded `SessionId`, so `live.has(id)` did not check
    against the harness actually installed here. The same file already uses
    `Map<SessionId, ...>` for the pending runner's maps two functions down, so
    this was its own odd case out rather than a deliberate choice. Runtime
    behaviour is identical — a brand is erased — but the port now type-checks
    against the running harness.

  - The tsconfig deliberately mirrors upstream's compiler options rather than
    this repository's stricter default. Enabling noUncheckedIndexedAccess on
    code never written against it produced ten complaints that were style, not
    defects; silencing them one by one would have made a port into a rewrite.

  - schemastery and zod are bundled rather than installed. The harness profile
    resolves only what it ships itself.

  - The ./invariant companion is dropped. It registers a no-op installer to
    reserve package ownership in the diagnostics registry, and its own
    docstring records that the package has no runtime invariant to assert.

  - dsh.plugin.json and README.zh.md are dropped: the first is read by
    `dsh plugin add`, which this repository does not use, and the second is a
    translation this repository does not carry.

Type-checking resolves the harness the same way @my-dsh/at-file does:
scripts/link-harness.mjs symlinks the INSTALLED harness into node_modules
before tsc runs, so the types can never drift from the deployment.

